===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|dwóh₁}}
From {{inh|en|enm|two}}, {{m|enm|twa}}, from {{inh|en|ang|twā}}, feminine and neuter of {{m|ang|twēġen}} (whence {{m|en|twain}}), from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*twai-}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*twai}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*dwóh₁}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|twa||two}}; {{cog|frr|tou}}, {{m|frr|tuu||two}}; {{cog|stq|twäin}}, {{m|stq|two||two}}; {{cog|fy|twa||two}}; {{cog|nl|twee||two}}; {{cog|nds|twee}}, {{m|nds|twei||two}}; {{cog|de|zwei}}, {{m|de|zwo||two}}; {{cog|da|-}} and {{cog|no|to||two}}; {{cog|sv|två}}, {{m|sv|tu||two}}; {{cog|is|tvö||two}}; {{cog|fo|tvey||two}}; {{cog|la|duō||two}}; {{cog|grc|δύο||two}}; {{cog|ga|dhá||two}}; {{cog|lt|dù||two}}; {{cog|ru|два||two}}; {{cog|sq|dy||two}}; {{cog|xcl|երկու||two}}; {{cog|sa|द्व||two|tr=dvá}}; {{cog|xto|wu}}, {{cog|txb|wi}}. {{doublet|en|duo}}. See also {{m|en|twain}}.

